course: dictionary
lesson: 12134
title: Committal: a serious formal step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A committal is a serious, formal step. The clues in the sentence show you which kind. «At the committal, the family stood beside the grave as the coffin was lowered.» Grave, family and coffin are clues about a funeral, so committal means the part of a funeral where the body is buried or cremated.
explain: «The judge signed the committal papers, and the man was sent to prison.» Judge, papers and prison are the clues. Here committal means officially sending someone to prison, court or a hospital. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: The word looks like commit, which means to promise yourself firmly to something. Committal can also mean that firm promise, but people more often use commitment for that meaning. When you are not sure, read the words around the word and look for the clues.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Committal» is a noun, and its plural is committals.
fact: «Committal» means the part of a funeral when the body is buried or cremated, with a final prayer.
fact: In law, «committal» means officially sending someone to prison, court or a hospital.
fact: Phrases to know: committal service, committal to prison, committal for trial.
exercise: «At the committal, the family stood beside the grave.» What does committal mean here? | A happy family party | A long walk to the church | *The part of a funeral when the body is buried or cremated, with a final prayer | The part of a funeral when the body is buried or cremated
exercise: «The judge signed the committal papers, and the man was sent to prison.» What does committal mean here? | Doing a school test | *Officially sending someone to prison, court or a hospital | Choosing a new hat | Being very tired after a long day
exercise: «The committal service was held at the graveside.» Find and copy the word that best shows this is about a funeral. | committal | held | was | *graveside
test: «The committal to prison was for three years.» What does committal mean here? | *Officially sending someone to prison | Promising to visit a prison | Leaving the prison gates early | Painting the walls of a prison
test: «Her committal to the team was strong, and she trained every day.» What does committal mean here? | Saying a final prayer | *A firm promise to something | Losing a game | Being sent to hospital
exam: Which phrase means officially sending someone to court for a trial? | *committal for trial | committal papers for a party | graveside prayer | committal service
